{title: Im Going Through}
{key: D}

{comment: Chorus}
[D]I'm going through, yes [G]I'm going [D]through,
I pay the price what[E]ever others [A]do
[D]I'll take the way with the [G]Lord's despised [D]few
I've started in Jesus and I'm [A]going [D]through.

{comment: Verse 1}
[D]Lord, I have started to [G]walk in the [D]light,
Shining upon me from [E]heaven so [A]bright;
[D]I bade the world and its [G]follies [D]adieu,
I've started in Jesus and [A]I'm going [D]through.

{comment: Verse 2}
[D]O there are many who start in the [D]race,
But with the light [E]refuse to keep the [A]pace.
[D]Others except it [G]because it is [D]knew,
But not very many [A]expect to go [D]through.

{comment: Verse 3}
[D]I'd rather walk with [G]Jesus [D]alone,
Have for a pillow, like [E]Jacob, a [A]stone;
[D]Living each moment with [G]His face in [D]view,
Than shrink from my pathway and [A]fail to go [D]through.

{comment: Verse 4}
[D]O brother, now will you [G]take up the [D]cross?
Give up the world and [E]count it as [A]dross;
Sell all thou hast and give to the [D]poor,
Then go through with Jesus and [A]those who [D]endure.
